* {{IPA|/t/}} preceding a high front vowel {{IPA|/i/}} is usually realized as an affricate sound {{IPAblink|tʃ}}.<ref>{{harvp|Scebold|2003}}</ref>
* {{IPA|/k, ŋ/}} tend to shift to uvular sounds {{IPA|[q, ɴ]}} when adjacent to {{IPA|/a/}}.<ref>{{harvp|Scebold|2003|pages=30}}</ref>

