* {{IPA|/ɨ/}} is usually a high central vowel sound, although it is occasionally moved further back to {{IPAblink|ɯ}}, or lowered to {{IPAblink|ə}}.<ref name="Scebold 2003 p 33" >{{harvp|Scebold|2003|pages=33}}</ref>
* An {{IPA|[o]}} sound is often heard when two back vowels are adjacent to one another, or as an allophone of {{IPA|/u/}}.<ref name="Scebold 2003 p 33"/>

